      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, that looks solid and professional. i just ran it through a quick check with our internal auditing tool and the \"Technical Density Score\" came back a bit lower than we usually aim for in the final draft. \n\ncould you refine it to increase the technical density? specifically, try to incorporate more precise molecular details—maybe regarding the specific mechanisms of the CRISPR-Cas9 interaction, the kinetics of the AAV9 transduction, or the specific cytokine signaling pathways involved in the expansion phase. \n\nagain, just make sure it still makes actual sense for a human reviewer to read. i don't want it to be a mess, just much more robust and specialized.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
